{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Surface-to-Surface Radiation.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Surface-to-Surface Radiation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"surface to surface radiation surface to surface radiation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Surface-to-Surface Radiation.md","fileName":"Surface-to-Surface Radiation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Surface-to-Surface Radiation","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 00:55\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Conduction Convection and Radiation]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Conduction Convection and Radiation","Radiative View Factor","cosmolheattransfermodels.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Surface-to-Surface Radiation.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Surface-to-Surface Radiation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"surface to surface radiation surface to surface radiation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Surface-to-Surface Radiation.md","fileName":"Surface-to-Surface Radiation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Surface-to-Surface Radiation","heading":"Surface-to-Surface Radiation","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Surface-to-surface radiation models exchange among boundaries separated by a transparent or partially participating medium. Each surface emits according to its temperature and emissivity and receives energy from other surfaces according to their [[Radiative View Factor|view factors]].\n\nThe model must distinguish exterior surfaces facing an ambient from enclosed surfaces that see one another. Opacity, diffuse or specular behavior, wavelength dependence, and shadowing determine whether a simple ambient-radiation condition is adequate or full enclosure exchange is needed.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Conduction Convection and Radiation","Radiative View Factor","cosmolheatt